 "title": "SLC26A4 and ZBTB16 Protein Interactions and Expression in Human and Mouse Cells",
 "summary": "This cluster is centered around the SLC26A4 and ZBTB16 proteins, which interact with each other and other proteins such as CUL3 and ROC1. SLC26A4 is expressed in human and mouse cells, including HEK293 and HEK293 Phoenix cells, and is involved in the regulation of IQGAP1 activity. ZBTB16 binds to specific amino acids and co-localizes with AQP2. The cluster also includes various methods and tools, such as Western blot, FRET, and MG132, which are used to study the interactions and expression of these proteins.",
